blurb = "Depicts a rock formation surrounded by serene waters in Oga Quasi-National Park on the coast of Akita prefecture. The rock are painted red by the rising (or possibly setting) sun.

This rock formation is called ryū-ga-shima (\"dragon island\"), possibly due to its resemblance to a dragon's jaw. Part of it collapsed during the 1939 Oga earthquake."
